# Same-origin proxies back to the Django backend.
#
# The browser must never talk to the backend host directly: a public page
# (rtutindahan.netlify.app) that fetches a tailnet address is blocked by
# Chrome's Private Network Access rules, and the backend hostname changes
# whenever the tunnel is re-minted. Proxying through Netlify's edge keeps the
# API, the Django admin and its static files on this site's own origin, so CORS
# and private-address checks drop out of the picture entirely.
#
# The upstream is the Cloudflare quick tunnel for kallisto-1:8000. Regenerate
# these three lines with `tindahan-netlify-sync` when the tunnel host changes.
/api/*     https://hdtv-commission-accepted-cos.trycloudflare.com/api/:splat  200
/admin/*   https://hdtv-commission-accepted-cos.trycloudflare.com/admin/:splat  200
/static/*  https://hdtv-commission-accepted-cos.trycloudflare.com/static/:splat  200

# Everything else is the SPA. The app uses hash routing, so no deep-link
# rewrite is required, but this keeps stray paths on index.html.
/*  /index.html  200
